<td id="S2.T2.7.77.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:-1.2pt;padding-bottom:-1.2pt;">
<span id="S2.T2.7.77.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:128.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">
<span id="S2.T2.7.77.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T2.7.77.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">LLM prompt construction function</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.7.78" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;">
<td id="S2.T2.7.78.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.2pt;padding-bottom:-1.2pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m83" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;" alttext="\rho(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;" mathbackground="#E9F3FF" mathsize="0.700em">ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;" mathbackground="#E9F3FF" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;" mathbackground="#E9F3FF" mathsize="0.700em">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;" mathbackground="#E9F3FF" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.7.78.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.2pt;padding-bottom:-1.2pt;"><span id="S2.T2.7.78.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;">Risk</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.7.78.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.2pt;padding-bottom:-1.2pt;">
<span id="S2.T2.7.78.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:128.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;">
<span id="S2.T2.7.78.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T2.7.78.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Risk score of a scenario </span><math id="S2.T2.m84" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E9F3FF;" mathbackground="#E9F3FF" mathsize="0.700em">S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.7.79" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">
<td id="S2.T2.7.79.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-1.2pt;padding-bottom:-1.2pt;"><math id="S2.T2.m85" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" alttext="\sigma(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" mathsize="0.700em">σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" mathsize="0.700em">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T2.7.79.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-1.2pt;padding-bottom:-1.2pt;"><span id="S2.T2.7.79.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">Risk</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.7.79.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:-1.2pt;padding-bottom:-1.2pt;">
<span id="S2.T2.7.79.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:128.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">
<span id="S2.T2.7.79.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T2.7.79.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Safety category label of a scenario </span><math id="S2.T2.m86" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" mathsize="0.700em">S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">UAVBench - Dataset Generation Methodology</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Designing a benchmark for UAV autonomy requires scenarios that are both systematically diverse and scientifically rigorous. To achieve this, we formalize each scenario as a structured tuple that captures simulation dynamics, UAV configuration, environmental disturbances, mission objectives, and safety constraints. Table <a href="#S2.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ II-F Comparative Analysis of UAV Benchmarks ‣ II Related Work ‣ UAVBench: An Open Benchmark Dataset for Autonomous and Agentic AI UAV Systems via LLM-Generated Flight Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a> summarizes the core mathematical notation used throughout this section.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-F Comparative Analysis of UAV Benchmarks ‣ II Related Work ‣ UAVBench: An Open Benchmark Dataset for Autonomous and Agentic AI UAV Systems via LLM-Generated Flight Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> presents the complete <span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">UAVBench</span> pipeline, illustrating the structured process for generating, validating, and labeling UAV scenarios. The framework begins with taxonomy-guided LLM scenario generation, followed by multi-stage validation that ensures schema compliance, geometric and physical feasibility, and safety consistency. Validated scenarios are then risk-scored and safety-tagged before being passed to an auxiliary LLM module that produces concise human-readable descriptions. The resulting dataset—composed of validated and labeled JSON files—is ready for benchmarking and simulation of agentic AI systems in diverse UAV mission contexts.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Scenario Schema Design</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The benchmark relies on a structured schema that ensures that each scenario is both syntactically valid and physically realistic. To make this explicit, we formalize the schema using mathematical notation and provide detailed definitions of all symbols. A scenario is represented as follows.</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\langle\texttt{name},\texttt{seed},\Sigma,\mathcal{U},\mathcal{E},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{X}_{0},\mathcal{M},\mathcal{T},\mathcal{O},\mathcal{W},\mathcal{C},\mathcal{D},\mathcal{F},\mathcal{L}\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">name</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seed</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\langle\texttt{name},\texttt{seed},\Sigma,\mathcal{U},\mathcal{E},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{X}_{0},\mathcal{M},\mathcal{T},\mathcal{O},\mathcal{W},\mathcal{C},\mathcal{D},\mathcal{F},\mathcal{L}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> defines the simulation parameters, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> the UAV model, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> the environment, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> the airspace, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> the initial spawn state, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> the mission, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> background traffic, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> obstacles, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> swarm teammates, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> the control space, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> safety thresholds, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> injection faults and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> communication constraints. The following subsections provide detailed definitions of each block.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span>1 </span>Simulation Setup</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The simulation setup controls the temporal structure of each scenario. It is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\langle\Delta t,N,f_{c}\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\langle\Delta t,N,f_{c}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> is the integration time step (s), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> the number of discrete simulation steps, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> the controller update frequency (Hz). The constraints are:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\in[0.01,0.05],\quad N\geq 600,\quad f_{c}\geq 10." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>600</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\in[0.01,0.05],\quad N\geq 600,\quad f_{c}\geq 10.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The duration of the mission <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is then:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=N\cdot\Delta t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=N\cdot\Delta t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These conditions ensure that each simulation runs for a non-trivial duration and at a temporal resolution appropriate for UAV dynamics. If <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> is too small, computational cost becomes excessive, while if it is too large, important dynamics may be missed. Similarly, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 600</annotation></semantics></math> prevents trivial short-hop scenarios and aligns the dataset with real-world UAV missions that typically last several minutes. The controller frequency bound reflects the operational limits of autopilots such as PX4 and ArduPilot, grounding the benchmark in practical system architectures.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span>2 </span>UAV Configuration and Propulsion</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The UAV block specifies the physical and energetic configuration:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}=\langle\tau,m,E_{b},V_{f},\xi,v_{\max},\phi_{\max},r,\mathcal{B},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{A}_{f},\mathcal{Z},\mathcal{P}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=\langle\tau,m,E_{b},V_{f},\xi,v_{\max},\phi_{\max},r,\mathcal{B},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{A}_{f},\mathcal{Z},\mathcal{P}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the UAV type, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> mass (kg), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> battery energy (Wh), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> fuel volume (L), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> energy source (<span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">battery</span>/<span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fuel</span>/<span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hybrid</span>), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> maximum velocity (m/s), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> maximum tilt (deg), and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> reserved energy fraction. The sub-blocks are: <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> battery model (e.g., hover power and coefficients), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> rotorcraft parameters (e.g., rotor count, disk area), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed-wing/forward-flight aerodynamics, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> sensors (renamed to avoid conflict with <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> payload.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Energy consumption is modeled as:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(v,\dot{\mathbf{u}})=P_{h}+k_{d}v^{3}+k_{m}\|\dot{\mathbf{u}}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(v,\dot{\mathbf{u}})=P_{h}+k_{d}v^{3}+k_{m}\|\dot{\mathbf{u}}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is hover power (W), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> drag coefficient, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> velocity (m/s), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> maneuver coefficient, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\dot{\mathbf{u}}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\dot{\mathbf{u}}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> the control-rate magnitude. The feasibility condition is:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}P_{k}\,\Delta t\leq(1-r)\,E_{b}\cdot 3600," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>3600</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}P_{k}\,\Delta t\leq(1-r)\,E_{b}\cdot 3600,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the discrete power at step <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and the factor <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3600</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3600</annotation></semantics></math> converts Wh to joules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Rotorcraft require rotor disk checks:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{h}\approx c_{\eta}\frac{m^{3/2}}{\sqrt{A_{d}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{h}\approx c_{\eta}\frac{m^{3/2}}{\sqrt{A_{d}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> aggregates propulsive efficiency factors and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is rotor disk area (m<sup id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>). For fixed-wing UAVs, aerodynamics are:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{D}=C_{D0}+\frac{1}{\pi\,AR\,e}\,C_{L}^{2},\qquad v_{\text{stall}}\approx\sqrt{\frac{2mg}{\rho\,S\,C_{L,\max}}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>stall</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{D}=C_{D0}+\frac{1}{\pi\,AR\,e}\,C_{L}^{2},\qquad v_{\text{stall}}\approx\sqrt{\frac{2mg}{\rho\,S\,C_{L,\max}}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{D0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{D0}</annotation></semantics></math> parasitic drag, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AR" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AR</annotation></semantics></math> aspect ratio, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> Oswald factor, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> air density, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> wing area, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{L,\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{L,\max}</annotation></semantics></math> maximum lift coefficient.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This block ensures UAVs are not arbitrary numerical constructs but physically realistic platforms. It encodes first-order aerodynamic relationships, preventing, for example, “impossible” rotorcraft from carrying large payloads with tiny rotors. By embedding both rotorcraft and fixed-wing models, the schema spans the full design space of UAVs used in research and industry. The inclusion of reserve fractions aligns with operational safety practices, which require UAVs to always retain energy for contingencies.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span>3 </span>Payload Taxonomy and Examples</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">UAVBench introduces a comprehensive payload taxonomy that reflects the diversity of sensing, communication, delivery, industrial, and defense systems employed across modern unmanned aerial vehicle missions.
Each payload is represented as</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\langle t_{i},m_{i},P_{i},C_{dA,i},\mu_{i}\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\langle t_{i},m_{i},P_{i},C_{dA,i},\mu_{i}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the canonical payload type (for example, lidar or thermal camera), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the payload mass (kg), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the electrical power requirement (W), <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{dA,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{dA,i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the projected drag–area coefficient, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mounting position (belly, nose, top, wing, gimbal, bay, or tether).
This standardized representation ensures that each payload contributes realistically to the total UAV mass, power consumption, and aerodynamic profile.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">UAVBench</span> taxonomy enumerates more than 200 canonical payload types, grouped into over 30 functional categories spanning the civil, scientific, and defense domains.
The taxonomy covers a wide range of mission contexts:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Imaging and sensing: optical, thermal, multispectral, hyperspectral, and advanced imaging such as lidar or synthetic-aperture radar.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Communication and networking: radio relay, cellular base stations, satellite communication terminals, and ad-hoc mesh nodes.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Industrial and environmental monitoring: methane and gas detection, pipeline inspection, and ground-penetrating radar.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Public safety and emergency response: search-and-rescue thermal cameras, fire-mapping systems, and emergency beacons.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Delivery and logistics: parcel and medical carriers, aerial drop systems, and life-raft deployment.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Scientific and environmental research: radiation detectors, atmospheric sensors, and biosensors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agricultural and ecological monitoring: multispectral and NDVI cameras, soil-moisture and crop-health sensors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Military and defense applications: electro-optical reconnaissance, laser designators, electronic-warfare systems, and CBRN detectors.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ III-A3 Payload Taxonomy and Examples ‣ III-A Scenario Schema Design ‣ III UAVBench - Dataset Generation Methodology ‣ UAVBench: An Open Benchmark Dataset for Autonomous and Agentic AI UAV Systems via LLM-Generated Flight Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a> presents representative payloads from these categories, illustrating the breadth of the <span id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">UAVBench</span> taxonomy and typical physical parameters used in simulation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE III</span>: </span><span id="S3.T3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Representative payload examples in <span id="S3.T3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">UAVBench</span> (excerpt from over 200 canonical types).</span></figcaption>
<table id="S3.T3.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T3.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-1.5pt;padding-bottom:-1.5pt;"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Category</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-1.5pt;padding-bottom:-1.5pt;"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Type (canonical)</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-1.5pt;padding-bottom:-1.5pt;"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mount</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-1.5pt;padding-bottom:-1.5pt;"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mass [kg]</span></th>
